1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,996
CHAPTER 9 — PIRATE OR NAVY?

2
00:00:03,346 --> 00:00:10,423
Jobs passed away in 2011, at 56. Tim Cook led Apple for the next fifteen years.

3
00:00:10,623 --> 00:00:19,854
For Apple's 50th anniversary in 2026, Paul McCartney played at its headquarters. A Beatle, after nearly thirty years of lawsuits over the name.

4
00:00:20,054 --> 00:00:27,362
That year a new chief took over, engineer John Ternus. And Apple launched its first foldable iPhone.

5
00:00:27,562 --> 00:00:35,023
Today it's worth around five trillion dollars, battling NVIDIA for the title of most valuable company on Earth.

6
00:00:35,223 --> 00:00:41,300
Jobs preferred pirates. But Apple is now one of the largest navies on the planet.

7
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,789
The question is whether it still has any pirate left in it.

8
00:00:46,739 --> 00:00:53,200
What do you think? What story would you like to see in the next episode? Let us know down in the comments.
